        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b033a127-e9f2-5011-b3dc-c5b8fcb4e1f0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eardwulf of Northumbria, Æthelred I of Northumbria, Ælfwald II of Northumbria, Æthelwald Moll, Æthelthryth, Alhred\n- Places: Northumbria\n- Topics: Northumbrian kingship, dynastic strife, deposition, assassination, reigns\n\nFacts:\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria was born around 762 and was killed on 18 April 796.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria was the son of Æthelwald Moll and Æthelthryth.\n- Alhred was deposed before Æthelred I of Northumbria possibly became king while still a child.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria ruled Northumbria from 774 to 779.\n- In 790, Æthelred I of Northumbria attempted to have Eardwulf of Northumbria assassinated during dynastic strife among noble families in Northumbria.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria ruled Northumbria again from 790 until he was murdered in 796.\n- According to one tradition, Ælfwald II of Northumbria reigned as king of Northumbria after Eardwulf of Northumbria was deposed in 806.\n- Eardwulf of Northumbria may have had a second reign beginning in 808 and lasting until perhaps 811 or 830.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
